faqs:
  - q: "How does the random name picker ensure fair and unbiased selection?"
    a: "The tool utilizes your browser's native Web Crypto API via crypto.getRandomValues with rejection sampling to eliminate modulo bias. Unlike standard Math.random algorithms, hardware-level OS entropy ensures uniform probability distribution across all entries. Every name has an equal mathematical chance of being chosen on each spin."
  - q: "Can I remove winning names automatically after each spin?"
    a: "Yes. Simply enable the 'Remove winner automatically after spin' checkbox, or click 'Remove Winner & Close' in the announcement modal. The tool removes the chosen entry immediately and redraws the wheel geometry for subsequent rounds."
  - q: "Does the wheel accommodate users with motion sensitivity or vestibular disorders?"
    a: "Yes. The random name picker respects your device's system-level accessibility preferences. When 'prefers-reduced-motion' is active, spinning animations are bypassed entirely. The tool computes the winning slice instantly and opens the winner dialog immediately."
  - q: "Is there a limit on how many names I can paste into the wheel?"
    a: "You can enter hundreds of names into the text box. The generator automatically calculates slice angles and fits labels on the wheel. Each slice remains mathematically distinct throughout the cryptographic selection process."
  - q: "Are my participant names stored on remote servers or tracked?"
    a: "No. All name lists, spin computations, and winner selections operate exclusively in local browser memory. None of your entered names are transmitted to external servers, logged in databases, or stored in URLs."
